      "axis_verdict": {
        "text": "These six markers describe one control loop. The pituitary signals the testes to produce testosterone, circulating testosterone and the oestradiol it converts to feed back to damp that signal, and binding proteins set how much of the hormone is actually available. A change in any one of them moves the others, which is why they are read together rather than separately."
      }
